check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6846231Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6853477Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6944489Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6953280Z ^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6954432Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6955365Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6955652Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6955969Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6956626Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6957088Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6957363Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6958239Z    if you are ready to continue.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6958662Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6959230Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6960010Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6960966Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6961478Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6961720Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6962049Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6962481Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6962735Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6963262Z    can use Nix.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6963539Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6963702Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6964031Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6968744Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6969562Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6975452Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6975943Z I will:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6976431Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6976729Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6977310Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6978027Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6978584Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6979084Z  - install Nix in /nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6979974Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6980520Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6981218Z    /root
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.6990286Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.7000327Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.7001021Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.7001838Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.7002217Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.7002573Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.7003106Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.7020124Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.7021511Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.7030220Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.7030976Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.7031832Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.7032106Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.7032371Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.7032666Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.7033005Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.7033563Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.7033850Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.7034023Z If you would like to
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.7034937Z see the output, try like this:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.7035261Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.7035564Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.7036091Z   $ sh ./install-nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.7036308Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:20.7036320Z 
