conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9648970Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9656624Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9743575Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9752409Z ^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9753135Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9754075Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9754462Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9754842Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9755697Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9756216Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9756627Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9757527Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9757826Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9758769Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9759351Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9759859Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9760344Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9760526Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9760730Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9760992Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9761209Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9761601Z    can use Nix.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9761752Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9761873Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9762042Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9762358Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9762820Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9764989Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9765189Z I will:
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9765493Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9765881Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9766704Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9767431Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9767910Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9768235Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9768546Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9768982Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9769363Z    /root
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9779907Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9780863Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9790359Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9791302Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9791816Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9792204Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9792794Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9807651Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9808659Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9816708Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9817417Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9818080Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9818340Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9818562Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9818808Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9819040Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:52:31.9819461Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
