conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1323753Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1323936Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1324663Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1325334Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1327135Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1327282Z I will:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1327428Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1327717Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1328140Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1328569Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1329062Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1329348Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1329656Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1330078Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1330458Z    /root
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1345716Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1346199Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1356402Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1356924Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1357199Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1358292Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1358995Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1378751Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1379837Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1389961Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1390703Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1391296Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1391578Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1391782Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1392003Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1392211Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1392675Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1392904Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1393038Z If you would like to
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1393309Z see the output, try like this:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1393561Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1393779Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:27.1394301Z   $ sh ./install-nix
