check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9525742Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9631149Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9641115Z ^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9641717Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9642553Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9643352Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9643730Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9644641Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9645269Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9645627Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9646407Z    if you are ready to continue.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9646790Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9647940Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9648961Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9649761Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9650359Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9650885Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9651186Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9651648Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9651986Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9652602Z    can use Nix.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9653053Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9653150Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9653312Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9653651Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9654095Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9656246Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9656415Z I will:
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9656713Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9657033Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9657689Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9658105Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9658492Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9658755Z  - install Nix in /nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9659035Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9659450Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9659893Z    /root
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9671329Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9671962Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9683569Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:14.9684102Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
