conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1449056Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1538859Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1547663Z ^[[0m
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1548271Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1548665Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1548835Z 
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1548981Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1549633Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1549958Z 
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1550164Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1550593Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1550792Z 
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1551559Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1551957Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1552280Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1552674Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1552807Z 
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1552938Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1553130Z 
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1553274Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1553632Z    can use Nix.
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1553782Z 
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1553918Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1554103Z 
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1554456Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1555012Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1560968Z 
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1561108Z I will:
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1561485Z 
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1562077Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1562589Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1563119Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1563563Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1563806Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1564015Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1564334Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1564620Z    /root
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1861633Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1862270Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1872404Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
conformance-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:22.1872967Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
