conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3333456Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3340711Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3440740Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3451027Z ^[[0m
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3451803Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3452487Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3452853Z 
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3453101Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3453914Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3454356Z 
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3454615Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3455565Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3455959Z 
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3456486Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3457197Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3458099Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3458540Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3458747Z 
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3459017Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3459372Z 
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3459682Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3460121Z    can use Nix.
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3460314Z 
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3460512Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3460705Z 
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3465233Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3465872Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3466330Z 
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3466498Z I will:
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3466773Z 
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3467049Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3467691Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3468236Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3468714Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3469125Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3469462Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3469929Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3470531Z    /root
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3478881Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3479717Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3490950Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3491638Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3492150Z 
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3492449Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3492953Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3513528Z 
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3515119Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3524519Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3525269Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3526046Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3526302Z 
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3526531Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3526818Z 
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3527108Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3527585Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3527846Z 
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3527987Z If you would like to
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3528473Z see the output, try like this:
conformance-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:39.3528697Z 
