conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1269853Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1278538Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1369049Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1378932Z ^[[0m
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1379546Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1380148Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1380444Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1380701Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1381440Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1381883Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1382453Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1383022Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1383282Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1383759Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1384496Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1385375Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1385861Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1386102Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1386539Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1386919Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1387186Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1387721Z    can use Nix.
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1387923Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1388077Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1388328Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1392442Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1393674Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1399935Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1400231Z I will:
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1400380Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1400541Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1401100Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1401637Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1402038Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1402298Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1402545Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1402911Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1403230Z    /root
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1413502Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1413992Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1424573Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1425264Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:21.1425602Z 
