conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8741293Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8748720Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8843601Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8853354Z ^[[0m
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8854124Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8854691Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8855012Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8855234Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8855959Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8856363Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8856627Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8857892Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8858297Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8858839Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8859505Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8860499Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8861007Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8861246Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8861627Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8862533Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8862822Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8863383Z    can use Nix.
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8863791Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8864016Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8864305Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8864743Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8865527Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8865952Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8866117Z I will:
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8866399Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8866618Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8867305Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8867980Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8868602Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8869109Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8869487Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8870085Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.8870614Z    /root
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.9142063Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.9142931Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.9152999Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.9153932Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.9154286Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.9155386Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.9174824Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.9175253Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.9175721Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.9183831Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.9187845Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.9188482Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.9188818Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.9189237Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.9189582Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.9189824Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.9190332Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.9190668Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.9190837Z If you would like to
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.9191295Z see the output, try like this:
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.9191569Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.9192078Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.9192656Z   $ sh ./install-nix
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.9192854Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:25.9192924Z 
